2. bk.wasm — BK Emulator for Windows, compiled form

   bk.wasm is the emulation core of BK Emulator for Windows 3.7 with its web
   layer, compiled to WebAssembly. Its source code is not part of this
   repository.

   Copyright (c) 2002-2004 Yuriy Kalmykov; gid and contributors.
   From the headers of the original source files:

     This code may be used in compiled form in any way you desire.
     This file or it's parts can't be redistributed without the authors
     written consent, but can be modified for your private needs.
     Providing that this notice and the authors name and all copyright
     notices remains intact.

     This file is provided "as is" with no expressed or implied warranty.
     The author accepts no liability for any damage or loss of business that
     this product may cause.

   bk.wasm also contains:
   - BkSound and FDDController from BKBTL, GNU Lesser General Public License
     version 3 or later (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html);
     source: https://github.com/nzeemin/bkbtl
   - emu2149, YM2149 / AY-3-8910 emulator by Mitsutaka Okazaki.

3. bk.ini — settings file of the original BK Emulator for Windows distribution.

ROM images of the BK computers and their controllers are not part of this
repository.
